With `--recursive-modules`, Rust refinements may extend extern classes with foreign
members and generated functions, methods and constructors, including function-by-method
bodies and locally named extern members with bodies, and introduce generic foreign
classes. Trait parents use the ordinary Rust implementation and upcast conventions,
including inherited default methods and erased ghost fields. Each class uses the refining module's foreign namespace. Generated
constructors, including those marked extern, execute after allocation through the
foreign type's zero-argument hook and receive their arguments once.
Own and inherited compiled fields and implemented members naming a foreign enclosing
path retain explicit rejections; a trait's proper methods must be wholly generated
or wholly foreign.
